JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOMINE NORIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA, SEISHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JINBO, HIROKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMINE, NORIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of forming quartz glass by pressurizing at least one set of opposing planes of synthetic quartz bulk by a pressurizing means, characterized in that an air-permeable elastic member is disposed between the pressurizing means and the above planes of the synthetic quartz bulk pressurized by the pressurizing means and the synthetic quartz bulk is pressurized by the pressurizing means via the elastic member, whereby it is possible to satisfactorily control the amount of bubbles remaining in the quartz glass formed body after formation to thereby provide a method of producing quartz glass having excellent optical characteristics with an excellent yield.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un procédé de formation de verre de quartz qui consiste au moins en la pressurisation d'un ensemble de plans opposés d'une masse de quartz synthétique par des moyens de pressurisation, caractérisé en ce que un organe élastique perméable à l'air est disposé entre les moyens de pressurisation et lesdits plans de la masse de quartz synthétique pressurisée par les moyens de pressurisation et la masse de quartz synthétique est pressurisée par les moyens de pressurisation par l'intermédiaire de l'organe élastique, permettant ainsi de contrôler de manière satisfaisante la quantité de bulles restant dans le verre de quartz après sa formation procurant ainsi un procédé de production de verre de quartz possédant d'excellentes caractéristiques optiques à très haut rendement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>